WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is based on real women
who started a choir.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a fair amount of them
were in the film.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.540 line:92%
-Oh, well, they were sort of

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, background artists
and stuff.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they -- So, our director,
Peter Cattaneo,

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
who directed "The Full Monty,"
he just wanted it to feel,

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:21.087 line:92%
you know, as real as possible.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.722 line:92%
And we were filming on actual --

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.893
in army barracks, like,
on their bases and stuff.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we were filming
in their houses,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, they were,
like I said, extras in scenes.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:37.670
And their houses were our
green rooms and stuff like that.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.506 line:92%
So we really got to know them.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:44.811
It's based on a -- or inspired
by a documentary here called

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.847
"The Military Wives Choir,
where they form this choir

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
while their spouses
were, you know, in Afghanistan

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.620 size:88% position:44% line:92%
employed in Afghanistan.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.689
And so, you know,
just to try and take their minds

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
off this hideous situation
they built this choir.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, I mean, in real life,
it became this huge sensation.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.130 line:92%
They had a number-one hit,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:08.334
and there's 75 military wive
choirs all over the world now,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
but our film just takes it u
to a point where they --

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if it's giving it away,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they have
this big final song.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.012 line:92%
-And you -- Are you a singer

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.614
Was that one of the things
that drew you to the part?

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I'm really,
really not a singer.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.785 line:92%
I mean, I think everyone -

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kristin thought
she was a singer.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was lovely.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, she was...

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.592 size:84% position:42% line:92%
She was like, you know,

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
convinced she has
a wonderful voice.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.528
And she does.
She's got a really strong voice.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:40.033
But by the end, her parts were
getting smaller and smaller.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But she just...

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
And me, as well --
No, I mean, I sang --

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, you know,
educated in a convent school

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.142 line:92%
so you're always in a choir,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
when nuns died, you got to -

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.348
if you were in the choir,
you got time off school

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go and, you know, sing
at their funerals and stuff,

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that was a good reason
to polish your singing skills.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:07.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
But apart from that,
I haven't sung.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.195 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You would incentivize

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
what would happen
if a nun passed away?

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah, I mean,
it was just --

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
God, I've gone really red now.
It was just a bonus.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.605 line:92%
It was like an added bonus

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's lovely --
It's lovely to sing, Seth.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, seriously.
-Oh, I see. I see.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is about the -- Yes.
-It is. It is.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.580 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It's a wonderful film.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
